From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 27 Aug 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ppc32: TryInlineTruncateDoubleToI must fall through to the
 DoubleToI stub on invalid conversions

The 32-bit branch (Rockwell lineage) clears FPSCR:VXCVI, converts with
fctiwz, and on an invalid conversion (input outside int32 range) sets
result = 0 and builds an EQ/NE condition in cr7 - but then ends the
function with an unconditional b(done). The cr7 comparison is never
consumed: the inline fast path "succeeds" for every input, the
DoubleToI stub fallback in TruncateDoubleToI is unreachable dead code,
and JS ToInt32/ToUint32 of any double outside int32 range returns 0
instead of its value mod 2^32.

The failure is total for bitwise ops: in "x & 0xffffffff" the mask
literal 4294967295 itself exceeds int32 range, so it converts to 0 and
the AND yields 0 regardless of x. This is how it was caught: npm5/npm6
name their install staging dirs .staging/<pkg>-<murmur3(realpath)>
(unique-slug seeded branch), imurmurhash's "(k1 * c1 + (k1 & 0xffff) *
c2) & 0xffffffff" steps all collapse to 0, every package hashes to
"00000000", and the four distinct ansi-regex versions in npm's tree
collide on the same staging path - the second bundled-dep rename dies
with ENOTEMPTY during destroot. npm7's arborist does not use staged
renames, which is why it installs fine on the same broken binary.

Fix: make the branch to done conditional (beq on the cr7 comparison),
so invalid conversions fall through and TruncateDoubleToI calls the
DoubleToI builtin, which implements the modulo-2^32 semantics via
exponent/mantissa bit-twiddling (verified endian-correct: it uses
Register::kExponentOffset/kMantissaOffset guarded by
V8_TARGET_LITTLE_ENDIAN, and the result store-back/reload offsets
match). The ppc64 branch gets its upstream beq(done) back; it is not
compiled in this build.

Generate_DoubleToI's own fastpath beq(&fastpath_done) is correct as-is:
beq defaults to cr7 in this assembler, matching its cmp.

After this fix (G5 verification battery):
  (0x123456789 & 0xffffffff)  -> 591751049   (broken: 0)
  3735928559|0                -> -559038737  (broken: 0)
  (-3735928559)|0             -> 559038737   (broken: 0)
  1e15|0                      -> -1530494976 (broken: 0)
  4e9>>>0                     -> 4000000000  (broken: 0)
  new (require('imurmurhash'))('test').result() -> 3127628307 / 0xba6bd213
---
--- a/deps/v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc
+++ b/deps/v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc
@@ -1811,12 +1811,16 @@
   addi(scratch, result, Operand(1));
   bind(&conv_ok);
   cmp(scratch, result, cr);
+  // Only take the fast-path result when the conversion was valid (EQ);
+  // otherwise fall through so TruncateDoubleToI calls the DoubleToI stub,
+  // which implements the JS ToInt32 modulo-2^32 semantics.
+  beq(done, cr);
 #else
   DoubleRegister double_scratch = kScratchDoubleReg;
   ConvertDoubleToInt64(double_input, result, double_scratch);
   TestIfInt32(result, r0);
+  beq(done);
 #endif
-  b(done);
 }

 void TurboAssembler::CallRuntimeWithCEntry(Runtime::FunctionId fid,
